    "report": "A25",
    "note": "The baseline implements \"which keys does this object govern\" three times with three answers. Default filling ignores key_enum, so a key the descriptor forbids receives a materialized default and provenance that claims it came from a default; node selection for resolution ignores key_pattern, so a key outside the pattern is still substituted. The Dart implementation applies the same governed-key rule in both places."
